.TH PIDDIGGER 1 "2026" "piddigger" "Blue-team forensics"
.SH NAME
piddigger \- live PID forensics TUI for blue teams
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B piddigger
.RI [ PID ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B piddigger
is a read-only investigator for a single running Linux process. It reads
.I /proc
to present process identity, open files (including deleted-but-open and memfd),
sockets, memory maps, namespaces, capabilities, seccomp status, threads and the
environment, runs triage heuristics, and watches a live activity timeline.
.PP
Optional, opt-in live capture wraps
.BR strace ,
.BR ltrace ,
.BR perf ,
.BR bpftrace ,
.BR tcpdump ,
.BR gdb " and " gcore .
Collected artifacts are written into a write-once evidence case with SHA-256
hashes and an append-only chain-of-custody log.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " NAME"
Color theme: thugsred, midnight, carbon, dracula, twilight, daylight.
.TP
.BI \-\-interval " MS"
Refresh interval in milliseconds (250-10000).
.TP
.B \-\-ascii
Use ASCII borders instead of Unicode box drawing.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-icons
Disable Nerd Font icons.
.TP
.BI \-\-case\-dir " DIR"
Directory to hold evidence cases (default: current directory).
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Run against a built-in synthetic process; needs no root or live /proc.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print one JSON snapshot to stdout and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-report
Print a plain-text triage report to stdout and exit.
.SH NOTES
Collection is read-only. Running as root or with CAP_SYS_PTRACE gives complete
visibility; otherwise some /proc entries are unreadable and findings may be
incomplete. Findings are investigative leads, not verdicts.
.SH AUTHOR
Kawaiipantsu for THUGS(red) <https://thugs.red>.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR proc (5),
.BR strace (1),
.BR bpftrace (8),
.BR gcore (1)
